ROOT_CAUSE: The MessagePort substrate passed directly, but ChannelAros still lacked runtime proof that Chromium framing, IO-runner dispatch, and attached-handle decoding agree.
FIX_REASON: Add a focused AROS-only core probe with two real Channel instances, early duplex writes, an attached PlatformChannel endpoint, callback validation, and orderly shutdown.
SCOPE: mojo/core/BUILD.gn; mojo/core/channel_aros_probe.cc
VALIDATION: Hosted 16 GiB run reported PASS framed=2 duplex=1 handles=1 shutdown=1 and exited zero in 4.91 seconds.
RISK: NodeController invitations and browser/renderer Process launch remain unproven; this test uses two endpoints within one Process and dedicated reader tasks.
AI_DECISION_CHAIN: substrate PASS -> focused Channel harness -> visibility failure -> AROS macro collision -> corrected include order -> framed hosted PASS.
